// Design rule: Rootstock public APIs express intent in library-owned types.
//   YES: Trigger-free predicates (BooleanSupplier), Command factories returned from builders,
//        RootstockState / RootstockCamera / RootstockGains / PoseEngine.
//   NO:  XboxController, Shuffleboard, SmartDashboard, NetworkTable v3, raw MotorController.set().

// Ship two artifacts from one source tree:
//   com.rootstock:rootstock-core:2026.x   (edu.wpi.first, Commands v2, Java 17)
//   com.rootstock:rootstock-core:2027.x   (org.wpilib,    Commands v3, Java 25)
// with a shared `rootstock-solvers` module (state graph, A*, ShotSolver, PoseEngine math) that
// depends on NO WPILib command types at all and therefore ports byte-for-byte.

// Pre-emptive shims:
RootstockGamepad pad = RootstockGamepad.xbox(0);   // maps to XboxController in 2026, Gamepad in 2027
motor.setThrottle(v);                          // name matches 2027 to avoid a rename later
